<\body>
  <tmweb-current|Contribute|Team><tmweb-title|<TeXmacs> Workshop July
  2025|<tmweb-contribute-links>>

  <section*|Place>

  <image|missenden-team.jpg|1par|||>

  The 2025 TeXmacs workshop took place from <strong|Monday July 21 until
  Saturday July 26, 2025> at <hlink|Missenden
  Abbey|https://missendenabbey.co.uk/>, Great Missenden, Buckinghamshire,
  United Kingdom.

  <section*|Scope>

  The workshop was dedicated to TeXmacs developers and users: those who
  simply want to learn TeXmacs better, those who want to participate in the
  development, as well as people who would like to promote TeXmacs in
  education, research and elsewhere.

  There were a few basic presentations on TeXmacs and its current
  developments, as well as more insight presentations about writing style
  files, plug-ins, and Scheme extensions. We also animated group discussions
  on various aspects of the software.

  <section*|Program>

  <subsection*|Monday><strong|Ongoing developments and high priority tasks>

  <\compact>
    <\itemize>
      <item>Refine the program of the workshop

      <item>Continuous integration, builders, testing, bug
      reporting<htab|><with|color|blue|afternoon, by Liza>

      <item>WebAssembly<with|color|blue|<htab|>Massimiliano>

      <item>Portable Linux packages via AppImage<htab|><with|color|blue|afternoon,
      by Liza>

      <item>Support for Android, iOS<htab|><with|color|blue|afternoon by
      Liza>
    </itemize>
  </compact>

  <subsection*|Tuesday><strong|Collaborative edition>

  <\itemize>
    <item>Jupyter plugin<htab|><with|color|blue|Jeroen>

    <item>The ongoing collaborative platform<htab|><with|color|blue|Robin>

    <item>Font system: simplification, automatic support of new fonts,
    colors, emojis, native OpenType math typesetting<htab|><with|color|blue|Massimiliano,
    et al.(?)>

    <item>Answering mailing lists<htab|><with|color|blue|Giovani>
  </itemize>

  <subsection*|Wednesday><strong|Towards integration of artificial
  intelligence>

  <\itemize>
    <item>The ongoing collaborative platform,
    demo<htab|><with|color|blue|Robin, Joris>

    <item>Plugin for AI chat interfaces, translations<htab|><with|color|blue|Joris>

    <item>Handwriting recognition<htab|><with|color|blue|Joris>

    <item>Grammar and text style checking<htab|><with|color|blue|Philippe,
    online, 11:00>

    <item>Backup and synchronization of the <TeXmacs>
    cloud<htab|><with|color|dark green|discussions>

    <item>Sharing computational sessions (?)<htab|><with|color|dark
    green|discussions>
  </itemize>

  <subsection*|Thursday<htab|>><strong|Applications, promotion and
  organization>

  <\itemize>
    <item>New pedagogic materials: GUI for exercises and exams (see for
    instance <slink|https://github.com/alexisflesch/texamator>), tables of
    variations, probabilistic trees

    <htab|><with|color|blue|Marc, Jeroen, Giovanni >

    <item>Tests and exams by <with|color|blue|Adrian, Marc>: WIMS, AMC,
    R-exams (?)

    <item>Promotion campaign (better promote existing features)

    <item>User wiki

    <item>Html and website export<htab|><with|color|blue|Joris, Max>

    <item>Allow users to easily distribute their own work (e.g. style files,
    plugin manager)

    <item>Organization of meetings dedicated to high school
    teachers<htab|><with|color|blue|Marc, Jeroen, Giovanni >

    <item>Mogan version and summer projects for
    students<with|color|blue|<htab|>Darcy, <with|color|blue|online 14:30>>
  </itemize>

  <subsection*|Friday><strong|Challenges for future development>

  <\itemize>
    <item>Plans for the evolution of the graphical
    library<htab|><with|color|blue|Joris, Max>

    <item>Accessibility of the web site, documentation, and GUI

    <item>Binary packages including all supported plugins for high school:

    python (sympy et al.) OpenAI ?, jupyter plugin

    geogebra (need interface, or maybe without)

    maxima

    R (but not used in high schools)

    julia (but not used in high schools)

    jupyter-client (interface with maxima and R)

    Name proposals: name of mathematician (?) do not include <TeXmacs>, work

    non-existing name, typo (?)

    <item>Organization of future work for high school:

    Dedicated skin

    Improve spreadsheets (make it more attractive)

    Improve interaction with other software: clickable objets to open
    external sofware and insert the results.
  </itemize>

